<%- include('partials/head') %>

<div class="page-head">
  <h1>Pricing</h1>
  <div class="meta">
    Screening is free forever. Premium is <%= price.symbol %><%= price.amount %> a month per
    server<% if (plans.includes('yearly')) { %>, <%= price.symbol %><%= prices.yearly %> a year<% } %><%
      if (plans.includes('lifetime')) { %>, or <%= price.symbol %><%= prices.lifetime %> once<% } %><%
      if (trial.offered) { %>, with the first <%= trial.days %> days free<% } %>.
  </div>
</div>

<% if (!plans.length) { %>
  <div class="notice warn">
    <strong>Card payment is not open yet</strong>
    <p>
      Checkout is switched off while the payment account is being set up, so nothing on this page
      can be bought right now. <strong>Everything free stays free and is working normally</strong>:
      the approval gate, keyword blocking, the audit trail and tamper detection do not depend on
      any of this.
    </p>
    <p>
      When card payment opens, every server owner running BotApprove is told directly, once. You
      do not need to check back or sign up for anything. Holding a licence key already? It works
      now and will keep working.
    </p>
  </div>
<% } %>

<section class="block">
  <div class="plans">
    <div class="plan">
      <div class="plan-head">
        <h3>Free</h3>
        <div class="price"><span class="amount"><%= price.symbol %>0</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="plan-note">
        No card, no trial, no expiry. This is the whole approval gate, and it is
        <a href="<%= repoUrl %>" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">open source</a>.
      </p>
      <ul class="plan-list">
        <% freeFeatures.forEach((f) => { %><li><%= f.name %></li><% }) %>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="plan featured">
      <div class="plan-head">
        <h3>Premium</h3>
        <% if (!plans.includes('yearly') && !plans.includes('lifetime')) { %>
          <div class="price">
            <span class="amount"><%= price.symbol %><%= price.amount %></span>
            <span class="per">per month, per server</span>
          </div>
        <% } %>
      </div>

      <% if (plans.includes('yearly') || plans.includes('lifetime') || lifetime.soldOut) { %>
        <ul class="price-options">
          <li>
            <span class="amount"><%= price.symbol %><%= price.amount %></span>
            <span class="per">a month, per server</span>
          </li>
          <% if (plans.includes('yearly')) { %>
            <li>
              <span class="amount"><%= price.symbol %><%= prices.yearly %></span>
              <span class="per">a year, two months free</span>
            </li>
          <% } %>
          <% if (plans.includes('lifetime')) { %>
            <li>
              <span class="amount"><%= price.symbol %><%= prices.lifetime %></span>
              <span class="per">
                once, for as long as BotApprove operates<%
                  if (lifetime.capped) { %>, <%= lifetime.remaining %> of
                  <%= lifetime.cap %> left<% } %>
              </span>
            </li>
          <% } else if (lifetime.soldOut) { %>
            <li>
              <span class="amount faint"><%= price.symbol %><%= prices.lifetime %></span>
              <span class="per">
                once, <strong>sold out</strong>. Email
                <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a> if you need one.
              </span>
            </li>
          <% } %>
        </ul>
      <% } %>

      <% if (trial.offered) { %>
        <p class="plan-note">
          <strong><%= trial.days %> days free</strong> on the monthly and yearly plans, then
          billing starts. Cancel during the trial and you are not charged. One trial per server.
        </p>
      <% } %>
      <p class="plan-note">Everything in Free, plus:</p>
      <ul class="plan-list">
        <% premiumFeatures.forEach((f) => { %><li><%= f.name %></li><% }) %>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">
    Priced per server, not per member, so a large community costs the same as a small one.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <div class="block-head"><h2>What premium actually adds</h2></div>
  <dl class="modes">
    <% premiumFeatures.forEach((f) => { %>
      <div class="mode safe">
        <span class="dot"></span>
        <div>
          <dt><%= f.name %></dt>
          <dd><%= f.blurb %></dd>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% }) %>
  </dl>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <div class="block-head"><h2>Questions worth answering upfront</h2></div>
  <div class="cols two">
    <div>
      <h3 class="q">What happens if I stop paying?</h3>
      <p class="a">
        The premium rows switch off and you get a message naming exactly which ones. The approval
        gate, your keyword blocklist, the audit trail and tamper detection keep running. BotApprove
        does not leave your server and does not stop screening bots over money.
      </p>

      <h3 class="q">Do I lose my settings?</h3>
      <p class="a">
        No. Your whitelist, keywords, approver roles and configuration are kept. Paying again
        restores everything with nothing to reconfigure.
      </p>

      <h3 class="q">Is there a refund?</h3>
      <p class="a">
        No. Payments are non-refundable, including partial months after a cancellation. Cancelling
        stops future charges rather than refunding past ones. If you are a consumer somewhere with
        a statutory right to cancel a digital purchase, that right still applies. See the
        <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="q">How do I cancel?</h3>
      <p class="a">
        From your server's dashboard, under Licence, choose Manage billing. If you cannot reach
        the dashboard<% if (portalUrl) { %>, use the
        <a href="<%= portalUrl %>" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">billing portal</a>
        and enter the email you paid with<% } else { %>, contact the operator<% } %>.
        Cancelling stops future charges and premium stays active until the period you already
        paid for ends.
      </p>

      <h3 class="q">How do I activate it?</h3>
      <p class="a">
        Redeem a licence key with <code>/license redeem</code> in your server, or paste it into
        the licence field on your server's dashboard page.
      </p>

      <h3 class="q">Does the free tier expire?</h3>
      <p class="a">
        No. There is no trial countdown on the core gate and no feature that quietly stops working.
        Free means free.
      </p>

      <h3 class="q">Why is the nuke bot database paid?</h3>
      <p class="a">
        Because it is the part that takes real maintenance: every submission is reviewed by hand
        before a bot is listed. The invite-and-approve gate is sound protection on its own, so it
        stays free.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <div class="block-head"><h2>Ready</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    Add BotApprove first and use it free. Upgrade later if you want the threat list and automation.
  </p>
  <div class="cta">
    <a class="btn primary" href="<%= inviteUrl %>">Add to Discord</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/login">Sign in to the dashboard</a>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/foot') %>
